WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:03.460
The Practice Fusion iPad app
liberates doctors from their desktops

00:03.460 --> 00:07.700
and let them spend more time on what
matters most, which is treating patients.

00:07.700 --> 00:12.200
The app works seamlessly with Practice
Fusion's robust free web-based system

00:12.200 --> 00:15.280
so that all patient information
that they've already invested in

00:15.280 --> 00:17.780
is available at the doctor's fingertips.

00:18.520 --> 00:22.240
The app lets doctors both review
and write medical charts.

00:22.240 --> 00:25.540
It makes it easy and fast for the
doctor to learn about their upcoming

00:25.540 --> 00:30.660
patient visits and to examine each chart
in as much detail as they need.

00:30.660 --> 00:33.700
This is how you use the
app during an appointment.

00:34.000 --> 00:37.300
All patients that are coming
in today are shown in the schedule.

00:37.300 --> 00:41.360
You can also see a quick summary about
each patient and why they're coming in.

00:41.600 --> 00:45.780
There's also a picture and quick demographic
information that lets you understand

00:45.780 --> 00:50.120
who the patient is, everything that the
doctor needs to prepare for the appointment.

00:50.600 --> 00:52.740
It's easy to learn more about a patient.

00:52.740 --> 00:55.240
The patient summary shows
all the salient information

00:55.240 --> 00:57.920
that the doctor needs on a single sheet.

00:57.920 --> 01:01.180
There's previous illnesses,
medications, and allergies –

01:01.180 --> 01:05.300
everything that the doctor needs to
understand the person's state of health.

01:05.300 --> 01:08.220
When the patient tells the doctor
about their health problems,

01:08.220 --> 01:12.120
the app makes it easy to note down
the information right into the system.

01:12.120 --> 01:15.600
One way doctors can enter
information is using dictation.

01:15.600 --> 01:19.500
With dictation, they can record and
transcribe exactly what the patient says,

01:19.500 --> 01:23.460
which allows the doctor to capture
a lot of information really quickly.

01:23.460 --> 01:25.720
They can also use Practice
Fusion's templates

01:25.720 --> 01:28.800
that they're using on the
web-based system, on the iPad.

01:28.800 --> 01:31.240
These contain lots of common observations

01:31.240 --> 01:33.900
that the doctor can put
straight into the chart.

01:33.900 --> 01:36.660
And just in case, there's an
option for manually typing,

01:36.660 --> 01:39.560
though we think that they
really won't need it that often.

01:39.980 --> 01:44.140
The information is entered into the patient's
chart on the left side of the screen.

01:44.440 --> 01:48.940
When the doctor makes a diagnosis, he can
enter it from a list of common diseases

01:48.940 --> 01:52.280
or type a few letters to find
the exact word he's looking for.

01:52.280 --> 01:54.660
The app also leverages order sets.

01:54.660 --> 01:58.920
These groups of doctors' orders and
prescriptions make it easy for the doctor

01:58.920 --> 02:03.400
to enter in a whole set of items
that are pertinent for this patient.

02:03.400 --> 02:06.920
With the iPad app, doctors can
modify the order sets on the fly

02:06.920 --> 02:10.900
and with a few taps, customize the
treatment for this particular patient.

02:10.920 --> 02:12.580
And the patient chart is done.

02:12.580 --> 02:15.160
The doctor didn't even have
to type a single word.

02:15.160 --> 02:17.020
This saves a lot of time and effort.

02:17.020 --> 02:20.820
The doctor doesn't have to spend
time writing in the chart after work,

02:20.820 --> 02:22.700
transcribing from paper,

02:22.700 --> 02:26.180
or trying to remember details
from a visit earlier in the day.

02:26.340 --> 02:29.900
Practice Fusion's iPad app
helps doctors be more efficient

02:29.900 --> 02:33.980
and increases the amount of time
and focus they have with their patients.

02:33.980 --> 02:36.280
This is modern medicine in action.
